      "payload": {
        "approvalEvidenceComplete": true,
        "findings": [
          {
            "claim": "The rewritten docblock of findCommentByMarker still documents the ambiguity return as { ambiguous: true, comments: [] } while the code returns the actual matched comments, contradicting the contract postMarkedComment relies on for detail.matchCount.",
            "confidence": 0.85,
            "description": "commentMarkers.js:54 says the multiple-match return has an empty comments array, but lines 83 and 101 return { ambiguous: true, comments: matches } with the matched comment objects, and postMarkedComment reads existing.comments.length to build detail.matchCount (the blocked-detail the triageWorker surfaces in its error message). A maintainer or future caller coding against the documented shape would mishandle matchCount. The PR rewrote this exact docblock (adding the pagination paragraphs at lines 47-52) but left the stale @returns line. Low impact: the only in-repo consumer uses the real shape, so behavior is correct; this is a doc/contract contradiction only.",
            "evidenceRefs": [
              "repo-read:packages/web/src/lib/commentMarkers.js@HEAD:L47-L56",
              "repo-read:packages/web/src/lib/commentMarkers.js@HEAD:L81-L84",
              "repo-read:packages/web/src/lib/commentMarkers.js@HEAD:L127-L131"
            ],
            "severity": "P3"
          },
          {
            "claim": "After this change the triage decision log still records decision:\"skipped\" with reason \"no labels to apply\" and a configUsed snapshot that omits auto_comment for label-less classifications, even though the same run now performs a GitHub comment mutation.",
            "confidence": 0.7,
            "description": "triageWorker.js:335/338/345 compute the audit decision purely from labelsToApply and configUsed purely from auto_label, but the new gating at line 358 posts/updates a marker-backed comment (postMarkedComment at line 364) for every auto_comment-enabled run. Previously a no-label, no-hint run performed no mutation at all, so \"skipped\" was truthful; the change makes the \"skipped\" audit state contradict actual behavior for every no-label triage (e.g., auto_label:false repos or labels filtered out by labelNames). The dry-run proof/dashboard language treats \"skipped\" as 'skipped mutation'. Impact is limited to audit-trail accuracy: the comment mutation is separately recorded in the managed-actions ledger via propose/succeed (lines 384-391), and no behavioral/idempotency invariant breaks. Partially pre-existing (needs_more_info runs already had this gap) but the change makes it the default path.",
            "evidenceRefs": [
              "repo-read:packages/web/src/workers/triageWorker.js@HEAD:L332-L346",
              "repo-read:packages/web/src/workers/triageWorker.js@HEAD:L348-L365",
              "repo-read:packages/web/src/workers/triageWorker.js@HEAD:L384-L391"
            ],
            "severity": "P3"
          }
        ],
